messages:
customer-jane: Hey team — we've got multiple customers reporting duplicate POSTs (double charges) when our service hits a 5xx and the SDK retries. Happened after a node upgrade.

josh-support: Sorry about that, Jane. Can you paste minimal repro and SDK/node/undici versions? Also any request IDs or billing ids you have.

customer-jane: Repro below (simplified). Node 20.5, @redwood/sdk v1.3.2, undici 5.22. Request ids: r_2026_01_42a, r_2026_01_42b (two hits).

```js
// simplified example we ran in lambda
const { RedwoodClient } = require('@redwood/sdk');
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });

async function send() {
  const payload = { amount: 1, currency: 'usd' };
  // wrapper that the SDK uses internally
  await client.post('/billing/charge', { json: payload });
}

send().catch(console.error);
```

josh-support: Thanks. Can you share the SDK debug logs (set RW_DEBUG=fetch,retries) at time of one of the request ids? Also is this happening on warm lambdas only or cold starts too?

customer-jane: Logs for r_2026_01_42a attached (pasted):
```
[2026-02-10T15:02:12.123Z] fetch start -> url=/billing/charge id=r_2026_01_42a
[2026-02-10T15:02:12.623Z] fetch timeout -> abort id=r_2026_01_42a
[2026-02-10T15:02:12.624Z] retry scheduled -> attempt=1 id=r_2026_01_42a
[2026-02-10T15:02:12.625Z] fetch start -> url=/billing/charge id=r_2026_01_42a
[2026-02-10T15:02:12.900Z] 200 OK -> id=r_2026_01_42a
```

maria-eng-sdk: Looking at that pattern — the SDK is reusing the same AbortSignal / body stream when retrying. In Node + undici combos where the body is a stream (or a Request with a non-rewindable body), retries can end up sending the same POST twice if the first attempt timed out from the client side but the server received it. This is a known class of issue.

maria-eng-sdk: Quick checklist: 1) Are you sending a ReadableStream or FormData as the body? 2) Are you relying on global fetch vs undici client directly? 3) Could you add an idempotency key header as a short-term mitigation?

customer-jane: We're sending JSON via SDK helper so body is stringified once, but the SDK wraps into a stream under the hood. We do not currently set idempotency keys. Global fetch is the polyfill in Node 20 (undici-backed).

maria-eng-sdk: OK. Two likely contributing factors: (A) undici v5 has subtle signal/Request transfer semantics that differ from undici v6+ and Node's global fetch in Node 20 changed some behaviors. (B) The SDK retry code didn't clone the body for each retry attempt. Workarounds: set idempotency key header (x-idempotency-key), or ensure body is recreated for each attempt (e.g., Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(payload))).

maria-eng-sdk: Minimal repro we used locally to reproduce the dup POST:
```js
// repro.js
const fetch = require('undici').fetch;
async function postOnce() {
  const body = JSON.stringify({ n: Math.random() });
  const controller = new AbortController();
  setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 400); // client timeout shorter than server processing
  try {
    await fetch('http://localhost:8080/billing/charge', { method: 'POST', body, signal: controller.signal });
  } catch (e) {
    // retry using same body reference causes dup when server actually processed first
    await fetch('http://localhost:8080/billing/charge', { method: 'POST', body, signal: new AbortController().signal });
  }
}
postOnce();
```

ops-anna: Do we have any automated rollbacks or refund flows we can trigger for affected invoices while eng investigates?

josh-support: Finance looped in, we can issue manual refunds for confirmed duplicate charges. Please DM me the charge ids and we'll escalate priority. :handshake:

customer-jane: Thanks — I've DM'd the two charge ids. Curious if this is a package version mismatch though — our infra team recently updated Node from 18 -> 20 and bumped undici during that push.

maria-eng-sdk: Yep version mismatch is the likely catalyst. Plan: short-term mitigation = idempotency header or disable retries for billing route (retry: { maxRetries: 0 }) until patch. Medium-term = SDK patch to clone body for retries and detect non-rewindable bodies and fallback to non-retry path. Long-term = recommend undici >=6 / Node 20+ tested matrix and publish compatibility note.

maria-eng-sdk: I can prepare a canary build (v1.3.3-canary.retries-fix) that clones body on retry. If you want, try that in a staging lambda and let us know. Targeting a canary today and stable next week.

customer-jane: Can we get the canary? We'll test in staging and report. Also please add an explicit doc note about billing endpoints and idempotency.

josh-support: Filed a support ticket and flagged finance. Ticket #SUP-2026-109. I also put a temporary mitigation: disabled automatic client retries on /billing/* in their tenant config.

maria-eng-sdk: Steps we recommend for customers hitting this right now: 
- Add x-idempotency-key header per request
- Or disable client retries for non-idempotent routes
- Or upgrade undici >=6 when practical

support-bot: Reaction :white_check_mark: noted. If you need the canary, DM maria-eng-sdk and she'll share the install command.

customer-jane: Appreciate it. We'll validate canary and confirm. Thanks everyone.

maria-eng-sdk: Follow-ups: I'll open an internal issue linking the repro (+ logs), and add automated unit tests to the SDK retry logic to ensure body cloning or retry disabling for stream bodies. Will post updates in this thread when canary is out.
